{{ state_attr('sensor.camera_motion_stale','summary') }}

Quiet beyond window: {% set st = state_attr('sensor.camera_motion_stale','stale') or [] %}{% set aw = state_attr('sensor.camera_motion_stale','applied_window') or {} %}{% set hs = state_attr('sensor.camera_motion_stale','hours_since') or {} %}{{ st | join(', ') }}

{% set de = state_attr('sensor.camera_motion_stale','door_evidence') %}{% if de %}DOOR COVERAGE (door-contact record from the engine log). A line marked FAILING means the camera covering that door repeatedly did not report its openings - direct evidence at the camera's own door, which outranks the discriminators below; its counts separate openings other cameras saw from openings nobody saw. An unmarked line means the camera DID fire at its door in the engine log: if its last-saw time is after it went quiet here, detection works and the loss is between Scrypted and Home Assistant, not in the Ring app settings.

{% for k, v in de.items() %}{{ '- %s: %s\n' % (k, v) }}{% endfor %}
{% elif de is none %}DOOR COVERAGE: door record not reporting (state file missing, stale or unreadable).

{% endif %}CROSS-CAMERA CORROBORATION (strongest evidence - this check reads only recorder rows, the motion events already recorded):
{% for k, v in (state_attr('sensor.camera_motion_stale','corroboration') or {}).items() %}{{ '- %s: %s\n' % (k, v.get('verdict')) }}{% endfor %}
FRAME DIFFERENCING (weaker - an outdoor scene changes by itself):
{% for k, v in (state_attr('sensor.camera_motion_stale','verdicts') or {}).items() %}{{ '- %s: %s\n' % (k, v) }}{% endfor %}
Per-camera detail (event age vs its OWN applied window):
{% for k in st %}{{ '- %s: %sh silent, window %sh, localized visual changes %s\n' % (k, hs.get(k), aw.get(k), (state_attr('sensor.camera_motion_stale','visual_localized_count') or {}).get(k)) }}{% endfor %}
'Localized' excludes scene changes that fired on several cameras within three minutes. That covers lighting transitions, cloud shadow and the first frame after a restart - but ALSO a person or vehicle crossing a group of cameras that share a path, so a discarded change is not always ambient. Read the two discriminators in order of strength: 'EVENT PATH BROKEN' is a proof and means the camera's motion settings/zones in the Ring app are the first thing to check. 'Cannot be tested' and 'inconclusive' mean exactly that - no conclusion, not an all-clear. A frame-differencing verdict of 'suspect' is weak on its own: a camera aimed at open ground generates guaranteed lighting change and can only ever read 'suspect'. Note some faults are PHYSICAL (aim, obstruction) and no Ring-app setting fixes them. This measures motion EVENTS reaching HA; the camera records to the cloud regardless. {{ now().strftime('%b %-d %-I:%M %p') }}.
